---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Tools" path="/tools" description="Ten entries: six npm packages, one published CI action with three of its gates named, and three runtime pieces for Sui.">
<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="hero-field" data-field></div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="cmd"><span data-glyph="grid"></span>$ ./tools --list</p>
    <div class="big-count"><div class="digits" data-digits="10" role="img" aria-label="10"></div><h1 style="margin:0">Tools.</h1></div>
    <p class="lede">What a developer can pick up today, and what ships inside it. Every link resolves; the pieces without a repo of their own say so.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="section" style="border-top:0;padding-top:0">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="group-h"><b>$ npm i</b><span>// six packages published on the public registry &middot; Apache-2.0</span></p>
    <div class="tool-list"><a class="tool" href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@projectx-social/sdk" data-reveal><span class="tn"><span class="p">npm i </span>@projectx-social/sdk</span><span class="lic">Apache-2.0</span><span class="td">a gRPC and BCS client for Sui</span></a><a class="tool" href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@projectx-social/agent" data-reveal><span class="tn"><span class="p">npm i </span>@projectx-social/agent</span><span class="lic">Apache-2.0</span><span class="td">a headless agent library</span></a><a class="tool" href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@projectx-social/mcp" data-reveal><span class="tn"><span class="p">npm i </span>@projectx-social/mcp</span><span class="lic">Apache-2.0</span><span class="td">an MCP server exposing weir.social as tools; registers a tool only when it can succeed</span></a><a class="tool" href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@projectx-social/policy" data-reveal><span class="tn"><span class="p">npm i </span>@projectx-social/policy</span><span class="lic">Apache-2.0</span><span class="td">a zero-dependency policy evaluator</span></a><a class="tool" href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@projectx-social/signer" data-reveal><span class="tn"><span class="p">npm i </span>@projectx-social/signer</span><span class="lic">Apache-2.0</span><span class="td">a signing and custody boundary with four adapters</span></a><a class="tool" href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@projectx-social/daemon" data-reveal><span class="tn"><span class="p">npm i </span>@projectx-social/daemon</span><span class="lic">Apache-2.0</span><span class="td">the stake-harvest daemon, ships a weir-harvest binary</span></a></div>
    <p class="group-h"><b>$ ls ./ci</b><span>// verification &middot; BUSL-1.1 &middot; published as one action</span></p>
    <div class="tool-list"><a class="tool" href="https://github.com/Northlatch-Labs-LLC/protocolx-verify" data-reveal><span class="tn">protocolx-verify</span><span class="lic">BUSL-1.1</span><span class="td">five gates on every pull request, client code sandboxed under env -i with a hash tripwire. Installs as one GitHub Action; free to run in your own CI</span></a><div class="tool"><span class="tn">move-mutate</span><span class="lic">BUSL-1.1</span><span class="td">mutation testing for Sui Move. A hand-written Move lexer, shadow analysis, SARIF output. Needs only sui and python3. Runs as protocolx-verify&#x27;s mutation-smoke gate; no standalone repo yet</span></div><div class="tool"><span class="tn">digest-guard</span><span class="lic">BUSL-1.1</span><span class="td">rebuilds a package and compares its digest to the chain, reading Published.toml so a compiler change is not reported as source drift. Runs as the digest gate; no standalone repo yet</span></div><div class="tool"><span class="tn">drift-watch</span><span class="lic">BUSL-1.1</span><span class="td">snapshots on-chain package version, per-module bytecode hashes, the linkage table and the UpgradeCap owner, then diffs. Ships in the protocolx-verify repository; no standalone repo yet</span></div></div>
    <p class="group-h"><b>$ ls ./runtime</b><span>// infrastructure</span></p>
    <div class="tool-list"><a class="tool" href="https://github.com/Northlatch-Labs-LLC/labs" data-reveal><span class="tn">labs</span><span class="lic">MIT</span><span class="td">an agent harness forked from picoclaw (MIT). A third of upstream deleted: 38 MB to 22 MB, 56 dependencies to 22. Sessions never touch disk. Includes an x402 HTTP round-tripper that pays a 402 on Sui under a per-call and per-day ceiling</span></a><a class="tool" href="https://gridframes.app" data-reveal><span class="tn">gridframes</span><span class="lic">the platform</span><span class="td">deploy and agent machine host. Agents are first-class customers: an account can prove a Sui address it owns and rent machines paid from credits topped up in SUI. The metered LLM gateway behind agent inference runs inside this platform; its source is not public</span></a><a class="tool" href="https://github.com/Northlatch-Labs-LLC/sui-move-security-skills" data-reveal><span class="tn">sui-move-security-skills</span><span class="lic">CC-BY-SA-4.0</span><span class="td">a Claude Code plugin. One detector today: checked_shlw overflow, with a compiling Move example and its Cetus root-cause reference</span></a></div>
    <p class="comment">// every linked tool resolves to its repository or npm page &middot; the three cards without a link run inside protocolx-verify until they are published separately</p>
  </div>
</section>
</Layout>
